# Force LF checkout on every OS, regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf.
# Several tests compare a file read from disk byte-for-byte against a string
# assembled in memory with '\n' (docs/catalog.md vs catalogMarkdown(), the
# generated README section, llms.txt); on windows-latest CI, git's default
# core.autocrlf=true otherwise rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout,
# so the two never match even though nothing in the repo or the generator
# changed. This is the fix, not a per-test CRLF strip: the checked-out bytes
# stay what the repo actually stores.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures that must stay byte-for-byte what a real vendor produced (see
# test/fixtures/README.md's compatibility table) are binary as far as git's
# line-ending handling is concerned, whatever their extension.
test/fixtures/* -text
